-- DICT-SEMANTICS §2's EXCEPTION to "projecting methods.m yields a directly-
-- applicable value": "a method whose OWN signature adds a constraint over a fresh
-- variable NOT FIXED BY THE INSTANCE keeps that dictionary ABSTRACT; projection
-- then yields a value still awaiting that dict at the call site." This is `Q_m`
-- in §3 W3's `m : ∀ā_C. C ā_C ⇒ ∀b̄ μ̄. Q_m ⇒ τ_m`.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived): `render : Debug b => a -> b -> String` carries a
-- method-level `Debug b` over a `b` the instance head `Box K` does not fix. So
-- the `Box K` dictionary's `render` slot cannot close over a `Debug` dict at
-- CONSTRUCTION -- there is no single `b` to close over. The dict must be supplied
-- per call site by §4 `var`, at whatever `b` that site instantiates:
--   `render (K 1) (2 : Int)` -> `Debug Int`   -> "1" ++ "/" ++ "2"     => 1/2
--   `render (K 1) True`      -> `Debug Bool`  -> "1" ++ "/" ++ "True"  => 1/True
--
-- OBSERVED: check/run/build all ACCEPT and print `1/2` then `1/True`. CONFORMANT.
--
-- The two lines are the whole assertion: they project the SAME method slot out of
-- the SAME instance dictionary and apply it at TWO DIFFERENT `b`. A construction
-- that had baked one `Debug` dict into the slot would answer identically on both
-- lines (or crash on the second), so the pair -- not either line -- is what shows
-- the method dict stayed abstract.
--
-- Added after an adversarial review (F2) found this clause neither covered nor
-- listed as uncovered. It is OBSERVABLE FROM BEHAVIOUR, so the gate's separate
-- "§2 dictionary record shape" exclusion (which needs the Core-IR dump) does not
-- cover it -- that exclusion is about the `{methods, supers}` layout, this is
-- about when a slot is closed over versus left awaiting a dict.
interface Box a where
  wrap : a -> Int
  render : Debug b => a -> b -> String

data K = K Int

impl Box K where
  wrap (K n) = n
  render (K n) x = debug n ++ "/" ++ debug x

main =
  println (render (K 1) (2 : Int))
  println (render (K 1) True)
